Detail: the `500` body carries only a log reference, so the cause is not exposed. The pet named by
the rest of the body was read back unchanged after the `id: null` update, so nothing is damaged;
the defect is the answer and, for the create, the missing id assignment. TC-PET-39 cites this issue;
the `id: null` variant sits inside TC-PET-33, which cites the issue about refused bodies being
stored.
